jobs.description:
Looking for a stable job with great pay and opportunities to grow?

Do you enjoy staying active and working as part of a team? Whether you already have experience in logistics or are looking for a fresh start, DHL gives you the opportunity to learn, develop, and build your career.

As a Warehouse Employee, you will help ensure that customer orders are processed and shipped on time. Together with your colleagues, you play an important role in keeping one of DHL's largest logistics operations running smoothly.

Experience in logistics is not required. We value your motivation, commitment, and work ethic above everything else.

In addition:

- You are available for day, evening, and night shifts;
- You enjoy physical work;
- You have your own transportation;
- You are a team player;
- You speak and understand English.

As a warehouse operator, you’re the key player in the logistics process. You unload trucks and containers, stack goods on pallets, and make sure everything is scanned, labeled, and shrink-wrapped correctly. You use internal transport equipment like forklifts and reach trucks to move everything quickly and safely. You count inventory, pick orders, and get them ready for shipping. You also help with value-added activities like packaging or labeling products. You’ll work full time (40 hours a week), mostly in day shifts. Together with your colleagues, you keep the warehouse tidy and safe. You work closely with your team leader and supervisor, and your day flies by thanks to the variety of tasks. Speed, accuracy, and safety are always at the heart of your job as a warehouse operator.

This is what we ask from you:

- You are at least 18 years old and have a VMBO level of education or equivalent working and thinking level;
- You have a good command of the English language;
- You enjoy working as part of a team;
- You live within commuting distance of Moerdijk and have your own transportation;

Are you experienced in a warehouse and ready to take the next step into a leadership role? Or do you already have some experience in supervising colleagues and want to further develop yourself as a team leader? Then this is your opportunity! Within a fast-growing and international logistics environment, you will have the opportunity to further develop your leadership skills and  take on more responsibility step by step.

As a (junior) Warehouse Team Leader, you will work alongside an experienced team and supervise a group of 10 to 12 employees. You will be visibly present on the work floor, supporting the daily coordination of operations. You work closely with the Supervisor and be given the space to grow in your role.

Your responsibilities include:

- Supporting the supervision and guidance of warehouse employees;
- Working on the floor to ensure smooth daily operations;
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and discussing them with your manager;
- Contributing to the improvement of work processes;
- Monitoring basic safety and quality regulations;
- Working with simple reports and developing basic Excel skills.

We are primarily looking for someone with the right motivation and ambition to grow into a leadership role within logistics. In addition, you have:

- Experience in a warehouse or logistics environment;
- Interest in supervising or guiding colleagues;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Basic knowledge of Excel or willingness to learn;
- A proactive and eager-to-learn attitude;
- Availability to work full-time in a two-shift system.

Have you not yet held a full team leader position, but do you have ambition and some initial experience in leading others? We strongly encourage you to apply.

Are you passionate about quality, compliance and continuous improvement?Do you enjoy optimizing processes and ensuring that quality standards are maintained throughout an organization? Then this position as Quality Specialist could be the perfect next step in your career.

What will you do?

As a Quality Specialist, you will be responsible for managing, maintaining and continuously improving the Quality Management System (QMS). You will support site management, ensure compliance with customer and regulatory requirements, and help create a strong quality culture across the organization.

Your responsibilities include:

- Planning, implementing and maintaining the Quality Management System (QMS);
- Ensuring quality governance and compliance across logistics operations;
- Promoting a strong culture of quality and continuous improvement;
- Coordinating internal and external audits and following up on improvement actions;
- Monitoring customer, legal and third-party quality requirements;
- Identifying improvement opportunities and supporting process optimization;
- Advising and supporting management and operational teams on quality-related matters.

What do you bring?

- Proven experience in quality management within a logistics or operational environment;
- Knowledge of Quality Management Systems (QMS) and audit methodologies;
- Experience with compliance and continuous improvement;
- Strong analytical and communication skills;
- A proactive, structured and detail-oriented mindset;
- Good command of the English language.

SamenvattingStart as an Order Picker in Nieuwegein and make sure Albert Heijn supermarkets receive their products on time. Earn €14.99 gross per hour and allowances for working in shifts. Stay active throughout your working day, work with a friendly team, and make a difference every day. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker at this logistics organization in Nieuwegein, you make sure supermarkets receive their fresh products every day. Using a modern voice-picking system, available in Dutch, English, Polish, and Ukrainian, you collect orders in the warehouse. You walk a lot, pick products from shelves, and prepare orders for transport. You work quickly and accurately, because the stores depend on you. The job takes place in a refrigerated environment (around 4°C), so it’s important you are comfortable with cooler temperatures. You’ll receive clear instructions through the voice-picking system so you know exactly which products to collect.
Your tasks:
- Collecting products using a voice-picking system;
- Preparing and organizing trolleys for shipment;
- Checking product quantities and quality.

This job is for 40 hours per week. Your shifts will be scheduled as follows:
- Morning shift: 05:00–14:30
- Night shift: 19:30–04:00

Over het bedrijfAt your new workplace in Nieuwegein, you’ll work alongside colleagues from different countries towards one shared goal: making sure supermarkets across the Netherlands receive their fresh products on time. The atmosphere is friendly and welcoming. Colleagues help each other when needed, chat during breaks, and always have time for a joke. Together, you contribute to something that people rely on every day.
Wat wij vragen- You have your own accomodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- You speak Dutch, English, or Polish;
- You’re physically fit and able to perform physical work;
- You’re comfortable working in a chilled environment (around 4°C);
- You’re flexible and willing to work week
